---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About Maddy, RIMO's public mathematics notebook.">
  <article class="simple-page page-frame">
    <header class="page-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">About Maddy</p>
      <h1>A public record of learning mathematics.</h1>
      <p>The notes keep the work that usually disappears: the example that fixed an intuition, the hypothesis a first proof missed, and the question left unresolved.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="simple-prose">
      <h2>What belongs here</h2>
      <p>Each article handles one mathematical question. Concept notes connect a definition to examples. Proof notes expose the step carrying the argument. Problems focus on strategy and failed approaches. Notebook entries hold work that has not settled yet.</p>
      <h2>How the archive is organized</h2>
      <p>Analysis, algebra, geometry, probability, and combinatorics provide broad coordinates. Series and prerequisites record the useful connections between individual articles.</p>
      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>The source, article history, and deployment process are public in the <a href={SITE.repository}>Maddy repository</a>. Open an issue when a statement lacks a hypothesis or a proof can be made cleaner.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
